cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or these results, please cite them as below."
type: software
title: "Explainable and hallucination-aware cross-modality learning from chest CT for X-ray disease classification: lesion-faithful bone suppression and Swin transformer knowledge transfer"
abstract: "Code, pre-specified analysis plans, Kaggle kernels, saved results, manuscript and thesis of three studies of CT-supervised models of chest radiographs: a counterfactual lesion audit and a twin lesion-invariance regulariser for bone suppression, a capacity-controlled test of bone-suppressed classifier inputs, and distillation of a 2.5D Swin CT teacher into Swin radiograph classifiers with heat-map, localisation and hallucination tests."
